   429|    <section id="techniques">
   430|        <h2>FUE vs. DHI vs. FUT: Which Technique Is Best?</h2>
   431|        <p>Modern hair transplants in China primarily use three techniques. Here's what you need to know:</p>
   432|
   433|        <div class="technique-grid">
   434|            <div class="technique-card">
   435|                <h4>FUE (Follicular Unit Extraction)</h4>
   436|                <div class="price">$1,500 - $3,500</div>
   437|                <p>Individual follicles extracted using a micro-punch tool. No linear scar. Most common technique in China.</p>
   438|                <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Most patients with male/female pattern baldness</p>
   439|                <p><strong>Recovery:</strong> 5-7 days to return to work</p>
   440|            </div>
   441|            
   442|            <div class="technique-card">
   443|                <h4>DHI (Direct Hair Implantation)</h4>
   444|                <div class="price">$2,000 - $4,500</div>
   445|                <p>Follicles implanted directly using a Choi pen tool. Higher density possible. No pre-made incisions.</p>
   446|                <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Patients wanting higher density in small areas (hairline, eyebrows)</p>
   447|                <p><strong>Recovery:</strong> 3-5 days to return to work</p>
   448|            </div>
   449|            
   450|            <div class="technique-card">
   451|                <h4>Non-Shaved FUE</h4>
   452|                <div class="price">$2,500 - $5,000</div>
   453|                <p>No shaving required — visible results immediately. Hidden extraction method preserves appearance during recovery.</p>
   454|                <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Professionals who can't take time off for visible recovery</p>
   455|                <p><strong>Recovery:</strong> 1-2 days</p>
   456|            </div>
   457|        </div>
   458|
   459|        <div class="warning-box">
   460|            <h3>⚠️ Don't Fall for "Unlimited Grafts" Marketing</h3>
   461|            <p>Some clinics advertise "unlimited grafts" for a flat fee. In reality:</p>
   462|            <ul style="margin-left: 20px; margin-top: 10px;">
   463|                <li>Your donor area has a finite supply (typically 5,000-7,000 usable grafts)</li>
   464|                <li>Extracting too many damages the donor area permanently</li>
   465|                <li>Ethical clinics recommend a realistic graft count based on your balding pattern</li>
   466|            </ul>
   467|        </div>
   468|    </section>
