    <!-- SECTION 4: Techniques -->
    <section id="techniques">
        <h2>Techniques: FUE vs DHI vs FUT</h2>
        <p>Modern hair transplants in China primarily use three techniques. Here's what you need to know:</p>

        <div class="technique-grid">
            <div class="technique-card">
                <h4>FUE (Follicular Unit Extraction)</h4>
                <div class="price">$1,800 - $4,500</div>
                <p>Individual follicles extracted using a micro-punch tool. No linear scar. Most common technique in China.</p>
                <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Most patients with male/female pattern baldness</p>
                <p><strong>Recovery:</strong> 5-7 days to return to work</p>
                <p><strong>China advantage:</strong> Advanced robotic FUE available at top clinics</p>
            </div>

            <div class="technique-card">
                <h4>DHI (Direct Hair Implantation)</h4>
                <div class="price">$2,500 - $6,000</div>
                <p>Follicles implanted directly using a Choi pen tool. Higher density possible. No pre-made incisions.</p>
                <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Patients wanting higher density in small areas (hairline, eyebrows)</p>
                <p><strong>Recovery:</strong> 3-5 days to return to work</p>
                <p><strong>China advantage:</strong> Choi pen technique mastered by top surgeons</p>
            </div>

            <div class="technique-card">
                <h4>FUT (Follicular Unit Transplantation)</h4>
                <div class="price">$1,200 - $3,000</div>
                <p>Strip extraction from donor area. Higher yield per session. Leaves linear scar but allows maximum graft quantity.</p>
                <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Patients needing high graft counts (5,000+)</p>
                <p><strong>Recovery:</strong> 10-14 days (scar healing)</p>
                <p><strong>China advantage:</strong> Scar minimization techniques reduce visibility</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="warning-box">
            <h3>⚠️ Don't Fall for "Unlimited Grafts" Marketing</h3>
