    <!-- SECTION 8: Treatment Process -->
    <section id="process">
        <h2>The Treatment Process: Step-by-Step</h2>

        <h3>Day 1: Arrival & Consultation</h3>
        <p>Your clinic picks you up from the airport. After check-in at your hotel (usually included in the package), you meet with the surgeon for:</p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 20px;">
            <li>Scalp analysis and hair density assessment</li>
            <li>Discussion of your goals and realistic expectations</li>
            <li>Hairline design with your input</li>
            <li>Final quote confirmation</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Day 2: The Procedure</h3>
        <p>Surgery day. Here's what happens:</p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 20px;">
            <li><strong>Morning:</strong> Local anesthesia administered. You remain awake but feel no pain.</li>
            <li><strong>Extraction phase:</strong> Surgeon extracts follicles from donor area (back of head). Takes 2-3 hours depending on graft count.</li>
            <li><strong>Lunch break:</strong> Most clinics provide lunch. You can rest.</li>
            <li><strong>Implantation phase:</strong> Follicles are implanted into pre-designed sites. Takes another 2-3 hours.</li>
            <li><strong>End of day:</strong> Clinic applies a light bandage. You're given post-op instructions and medications.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Total time:</strong> 4-8 hours (depending on graft count)</p>

        <h3>Day 3: First Wash & Check-up</h3>
        <p>Return to clinic for your first gentle hair wash and post-op examination. Surgeon checks for any complications. Most patients fly home the same day or next day.</p>

        <h3>Week 1-2: Early Recovery</h3>
        <p>Redness and scabbing are normal. Avoid:</p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 20px;">
            <li>Heavy exercise (2-3 weeks)</li>
            <li>Direct sunlight on scalp</li>
            <li>Swimming pools</li>
            <li>Touching or scratching the grafts</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Months 3-12: The Waiting Game</h3>
        <p>Initial hair growth starts around month 3. Final results visible at 10-12 months. The transplanted hair will initially fall out (shock loss) — this is normal. New hair grows back from the follicles.</p>
    </section>

